<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Suharto</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1921">1921</a>–<a href="/years/2008">2008</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Suharto was an Indonesian army general who took power after the failed coup of 1965, during mass killings of alleged communists, and was president from 1967 to 1998. His New Order regime brought rapid economic growth and stability but also the invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-timor">East Timor</a>, repression and vast corruption. The Asian financial crisis and mass protests forced him to resign in 1998.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/suharto.jpg" alt="Suharto" width="320" height="410" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: State Secretariat of the Republic of Indonesia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:President_Suharto,_1993.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>After the massacre of more than 200 demonstrators in 1991 and <b>Suharto</b>'s fall, a UN-supervised referendum in August 1999 voted clearly for independence; pro-integration militias backed by elements of the Indonesian military answered with violence until UNTAET took over on 25 October 1999.</blockquote><a href="/empire/east-timor">East Timor · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Under <b>Suharto</b>, oil revenues, the Green Revolution in rice, which brought self-sufficiency in 1984, and later export manufacturing raised incomes sharply and reduced poverty, while the transmigration programme moved millions of settlers from Java to the outer islands.</blockquote><a href="/empire/indonesia">Indonesia · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>…Confrontation of 1963–1966, when Indonesia under Sukarno sent raiders across the Borneo border and landed small parties on the peninsula; Commonwealth forces, including British Gurkha battalions, defeated the incursions in a largely secret jungle war, and the conflict ended after <b>Suharto</b>'s rise with an agreement in August 1966.</blockquote><a href="/empire/malaysia">Malaysia · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Its leaders have ranged from <b>Suharto</b>, a militaristic anti-communist, to Nelson Mandela, a democratic socialist, united by a declared commitment to world peace and security.</blockquote><a href="/movement/non-aligned-movement">Non-Aligned Movement · Aims</a></li><li><blockquote>From the 1980s democracy returned across Latin America, South Korea adopted direct presidential elections in 1987 after mass protests, Indonesia rebuilt its presidency after the fall of <b>Suharto</b> in 1998, and many of the states that emerged from the Soviet Union in 1991 chose presidential systems.</blockquote><a href="/government/presidential-democracy">Presidential democracy · Through History</a></li><li><blockquote>Augusto Pinochet’s rule in Chile used authoritarian means to secure investment, bringing growth and high inequality, and <b>Suharto</b>’s extirpation of the Communist Party of Indonesia allowed capitalism to expand there.</blockquote><a href="/ideology/capitalism">Capitalism · In Power</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Kemusuk, in what is now <a href="/countries/indonesia">Indonesia</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jakarta">Jakarta</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/indonesia">Indonesia</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=-7.82,110.28&amp;year=1977" aria-label="Kemusuk on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7600 2456 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Suharto"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8050 2726h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8050 2726h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=-7.82,110.28&amp;year=1977">What was here in 1977? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
